/*  A small map of the world's land, used to draw the particle Earth.
    720 x 360 pixels (half a degree each), one bit per pixel, 1 = land.
    Made from Natural Earth (public domain, naturalearthdata.com) via the
    world-atlas package.

    "colors" holds Earth's real land colours (forests, deserts, mountains,
    ice) for each land pixel, as a 256-colour palette plus one index per
    land pixel, row by row. Sampled from NASA's Blue Marble Next Generation
    (July 2004, cloud-free; credit: NASA Earth Observatory), averaging only
    the Blue Marble pixels inside each land pixel.

    "detail" holds one byte per land pixel (same order): the city lights at
    night in the high 4 bits, from NASA's Black Marble 2016 (credit: NASA
    Earth Observatory, Suomi NPP VIIRS data), and the height in the low 4
    bits, from NOAA's ETOPO 2022 global relief model (CC0; ice-sheet
    surface, 0 to 5,000 m). The city lights are modern, so dates far from
    today show today's lights.

    Rebuilt with tools/earthsources.py (which runs landcolors.py and
    landdetail.py).

    You don't need to edit this file.
*/
window.YOU_ARE_HERE_EARTH_LAND = {
  width: 720,
  height: 360,
  data: "",
  // Real land colours, one palette index per land pixel (row by row).
  colors: {
    palette: "",
    data: "",
  },
  // City lights (high 4 bits) and height (low 4 bits), one byte per land pixel.
  detail: "",
};
